  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="44">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 44</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="44" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="272" ed="#robertson"/>Ne prenge hum nam [nu]l en conté ne defors, d'ici qu'il eit tres foiz demandé dreit el hundred u el conté.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="273" ed="#robertson"/>No-one shall make distraint of property either in the county court or outside it, until he has demanded justice three times in the hundred or in the county courts.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="517"><ref target="clause:IICn_19">II Cn 19</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 19</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 272–273 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text (K–M) not yet added</note>
      </div>
    </body>
